Theorem RL-15: ExtentClass is representation-owned evidence

  Preconditions:
    - AIMS supplies AllocationFacts.
    - Representation analysis separately supplies ExtentClass.
    - ProjectionInput pairs the two products without merging their authority.

  Soundness property:
    Forall AllocationFacts F and extents E1, E2:

      (P1) ProjectionInput(F, E1).facts = F.

      (P2) ProjectionInput(F, E2).facts = F.

    Runtime-sized evidence can constrain a physical plan but cannot mutate the
    frozen AIMS fact product.

  Proof obligation:
    Definitional projection plus a negative witness that changing ExtentClass
    never changes AllocationFacts.

    Part (P1/P2) - extent seam:
      StaticShape -> same AllocationFacts
      RuntimeSized -> same AllocationFacts
      Coverage gate: 2 extent cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl15_extent_seam;
        ExtentClass and AllocationFacts authority separation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-15 because StaticShape and RuntimeSized ExtentClass evidence remain separate from immutable AllocationFacts
